        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Own Wood", "{DL} says the wood came from {D.his} land.")],
        role: "Wood seller",
        exam: [.direct("What is your business?", "\"I sell firewood by the cord from stacks along the road at my property.\""), .direct("What was taken?", "\"Several stacks, about two hundred dollars of seasoned oak, gone overnight.\""), .direct("How did you learn who took it?", "\"A gas station camera a mile away caught a pickup stacked high with wood heading toward town.\""), .direct("What does the video show?", "\"A truck with split oak stacked above the cab and a license plate readable under the light.\""), .direct("Whose truck is it?", "\"The plate matches a truck registered to {DL}.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said the wood came from {D.his} own land and that {D.he} had cut it last season.\""), .cross("Many people sell wood from trucks?", "\"Yes, there are a lot of wood sellers in the county.\""), .cross("The wood on the video can't be identified?", "\"Not by itself. It looks like split oak, but so does a lot of wood.\""), .cross("You saw your wood in {DL}'s yard?", "\"I saw a stack there that looked like mine, but I can't prove which it was.\""), .cross("You mark your wood?", "\"I stamp the ends of some pieces, and a few of the pieces in {DL}'s stack had my mark.\""), .cross("{DL} has a woodlot?", "\"Yes, a small one behind the house.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took firewood again.", "Own wood."),
        allocution: "\"That wood came off my own land, and I stacked it myself over two summers. I know the seller sees it differently, and I respect that {V.he} lost a lot of work. But I can't say I took something that I believe was mine. I'm asking the court to give my explanation the same weight as the bark stamps.\"",
        truths: ("Bark stamps matched.", "{DL} has no trees."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did the wood come from?", "\"Part of it came from my own woodlot, and part I bought from a man down the road.\""), .direct("Did you take wood from the seller's stacks?", "\"No. I never went to that property. I don't know the place.\""), .direct("Why was your truck stacked so high?", "\"I had a big load to deliver, and I was running late, so I stacked it as tall as I could.\""), .direct("Why were you on that road?", "\"I drive it every week to deliver to two customers on the other side of town.\""), .direct("What did you tell the deputy?", "\"I told {OFF.him} where I bought the wood and offered to show receipts and my woodlot.\""), .direct("What would you tell the seller?", "\"I'm sorry for the loss. I didn't take it, and I hope the receipts show that.\""), .cross("You've been charged over wood before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I understand why you doubt me. That's why I kept my receipts this time.\""), .cross("A few pieces in your stack have the seller's mark?", "\"I heard that, and I can't explain it. The man I bought from may have mixed some in.\""), .cross("The man you bought from has a name?", "\"Yes, and I'll give it to the deputy so he can be asked.\""), .cross("You hauled wood that night?", "\"I hauled wood most nights that week. It was a busy season.\""), .cross("You'll let deputies compare the stacks?", "\"Yes, any time. I have nothing to hide.\"")],
        openings: ("A seller lost several stacks of seasoned oak, about $200 of firewood, overnight, and a gas station camera shows {D}'s truck stacked high, and {DL} had stood in this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say the wood in the truck came from {D}'s own land, cut and stacked by {D}. {D} hauls firewood for a living and has no reason to take anyone else's."),
