        timeline: [(0, "2 a.m.: the truck loads."), (1, "The seller sees empty racks.")],
        identified: "Gas Station Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let tillAgain2 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.tillAgain2",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Bait Shop Drawer Emptied Again"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole $190 belonging to {V}, a bait shop, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, A different shop's drawer was emptied while the clerk stepped away, and {D} was the only customer.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Counter Camera", "{D} opens the drawer.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Change", "{DL} says {D.he} was making change.")],
        role: "Clerk",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job at the shop?", "\"I work the counter at a bait and tackle shop, and I'm usually the only person there on weekday afternoons.\""), .direct("What happened that afternoon?", "\"I stepped into the back to bring out a cooler of minnows, and when I came back the register drawer was open.\""), .direct("What was missing?", "\"One hundred ninety dollars in cash, mostly twenties, which I had counted when I started my shift that morning.\""), .direct("Who was in the shop?", "\"Only {DL}, who had come in a few minutes earlier to ask about line and was standing at the counter.\""), .direct("What does the counter camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} reaching over the counter, opening the drawer, and taking bills while I was in the back.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say about it?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} was only making change for a customer who wasn't there and that no money was taken.\""), .cross("You weren't at the counter when it happened?", "\"No, I was in the storeroom with the door half closed, so I didn't see any of it live.\""), .cross("The video angle is from above the door?", "\"It is, so we see {DL}'s back and arm more than {D.his} hands.\""), .cross("The cash was never found on {DL}?", "\"Deputies searched {D.him} that afternoon and found about forty dollars, but that could have been {D.his} own.\""), .cross("Other customers come in during the day?", "\"Yes, there are a few regulars, but on that afternoon no one else came in until after I found the drawer.\""), .cross("You didn't count the drawer before closing?", "\"I counted it right after I found it open, which is how I knew about the one hundred ninety dollars.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} emptied the till again.", "Making change."),
        allocution: "\"I was only getting change for a bill, and I reached into that drawer out of habit from working retail years ago. That was a foolish thing to do in someone else's shop. I'm sorry to the clerk who had to explain the shortage to the owner. I wish I had just waited at the counter.\"",
        truths: ("The bills were folded in {DL}'s pocket.", "{DL} bought no bait."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you open the register drawer?", "\"I thought the clerk had stepped out for a minute and I wanted to make change for a twenty so I could buy bait.\""), .direct("Did you take any money from it?", "\"No, I never took a dollar from that drawer. I only looked inside and then stepped back when I realized how it would seem.\""), .direct("Why would you reach over the counter?", "\"I've been to that shop many times and the old owner used to let customers help themselves, so I assumed that was normal.\""), .direct("What did you have in your pockets when deputies searched you?", "\"About forty dollars of my own money from a paycheck I cashed that morning, along with my keys and phone.\""), .direct("What did you do after the clerk came back?", "\"I told the clerk I'd been waiting for change and asked for help, and I stayed in the shop until the deputy arrived.\""), .direct("What would you tell the owner of the shop?", "\"I'm sorry for the misunderstanding, and I should never have touched the drawer without the clerk standing right there.\""), .cross("Since you say you didn't take anything, how do you explain the missing cash?", "\"I can't explain it. All I know is I didn't take it, and I wish I hadn't gone near that drawer.\""), .cross("Reaching into someone's register isn't how a customer makes change, is it?", "\"No, and I can see that now. At the time I was thinking only about getting my bait and leaving.\""), .cross("You stayed in the shop after the clerk came back?", "\"I did, because I had nothing to hide and I wanted to clear it up before anyone assumed the worst.\""), .cross("Your own forty dollars could be mixed up with the shop's money?", "\"It could be, but I know my bills came from the bank that morning and I still have the withdrawal slip.\""), .cross("Will you show the court that slip?", "\"Yes, I have it in my wallet and I'm happy to hand it over so the court can see the time stamp.\"")],
        openings: ("A clerk at a bait shop stepped into the back for a cooler of minnows and came back to find the register drawer open, with {D} the only customer, and the counter camera shows {D} open the drawer, and {DL} had already appeared here in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say {D} was making change and a stack of bills was in the drawer. {D} did not take anything."),
        closings: ("The counter camera shows {D} open the drawer while the clerk was in the back, and since {PRIOR}, {DL} could not have missed what that means in a small shop with no one at the counter.", "Making change at a counter is not theft, and no one counted the drawer before or after {D} touched it. The State must prove {D} took money and not merely that {D} stood at the register."),
        timeline: [(0, "The clerk steps out."), (0, "The drawer opens.")],
        identified: "Counter Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let cartsAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.cartsAgain",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Carts Found in Creek After Earlier Case"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, shopping carts, causing damage of $700, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, Nine carts were pushed into a creek behind a different store, and a camera showed {D}.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Security Camera", "{D} pushes carts.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Dare", "{DL} says friends dared {D.him}.")],
        role: "Store manager",
        exam: [.direct("What is your position at the store?", "\"I'm the store manager, and I'm responsible for the building, the parking lot, and the carts we keep outside the entrance.\""), .direct("What did you find that morning?", "\"Nine of our shopping carts were lying in the creek behind the store, some of them bent and one with a broken frame.\""), .direct("What did it cost?", "\"About seven hundred dollars to replace or repair the carts, plus the time our workers spent pulling them out of the water.\""), .direct("What does the security camera show?", "\"It shows several people pushing carts across the back lot toward the creek bank, and one of them is clearly {DL}.\""), .direct("How do you know it was {DL}?", "\"The camera caught {D.his} face when {D.he} walked under the light at the edge of the lot, and an employee recognized {D.him}.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say about this?", "\"{D.He} said some friends dared {D.him} to do it and that {D.he} didn't think it would cost the store anything.\""), .cross("There were others on the video besides {DL}?", "\"Yes, at least two other people, but they stayed farther from the light and we haven't identified them.\""), .cross("{DL} didn't break any of the carts personally?", "\"I can't say who bent which cart. The video shows {D.him} pushing at least three of them into the water.\""), .cross("The creek isn't very deep, is it?", "\"It's only a couple of feet at that bend, so the carts were easy to find and pull out.\""), .cross("The store has had cart thefts before?", "\"Occasionally, but this was the first time someone pushed that many carts into the creek at once.\""), .cross("{DL} came back to help the next day?", "\"No, I never saw {D.him} again until the sheriff's office gave me the name.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} dumped carts again.", "A dare."),
        allocution: "\"It was a dare, and I was embarrassed the moment the first cart rolled into that creek. I pushed a few, not nine, but I let the others do it too, and I'm ashamed of that. The store has to fish those carts out and pay for them. I'm sorry, and I'll work off whatever it takes to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("Photos show {DL} laughing.", "The camera was hidden."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you at the store behind the lot that night?", "\"Yes, I was with a couple of friends and we were walking through the lot after the movie let out.\""), .direct("Did you push shopping carts into the creek?", "\"I pushed a few of them. My friends dared me to see how far they would roll, and I did it without thinking.\""), .direct("Did you think about the cost to the store?", "\"Not at all. I thought of them as old carts that would just be picked up, and I didn't picture the damage.\""), .direct("Who were the others with you?", "\"They're friends from school, and I'd rather not name them, but I'm not blaming them for what I did.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"We left right away, and I felt guilty by the time I got home. I knew I'd done something stupid.\""), .direct("What would you tell the store manager?", "\"I'm sorry for the damage and the work it caused, and I'll pay for the carts and help clean up if you want.\""), .cross("You're an adult, so why did a dare convince you?", "\"That's no excuse, and I know it. I wanted to look bold in front of my friends and I made a bad call.\""), .cross("The carts had to be pulled out of cold water, didn't they?", "\"I imagine so, and I regret that a store worker had to do that because of me.\""), .cross("Do you think a dare makes it less serious?", "\"No. It doesn't change what I did, and I'm not asking the court to treat it as a joke.\""), .cross("Can you pay seven hundred dollars?", "\"I can pay part of it now and the rest over a few months from my job, if the court allows it.\""), .cross("Will you stay away from that store's back lot?", "\"Yes, and I'll stay out of any place where I could be tempted to pull a stunt like that again.\"")],
        openings: ("Nine shopping carts were found in a creek behind a different store, some bent and one with a broken frame, and the security camera shows {D} pushing them, and this was not {DL}'s first time here, after {PRIOR} in {PRIORDATE}.", "The defense will say friends dared {D} to push the carts and it was a stupid, thoughtless joke, not a plan to ruin anything. {D} did not mean to break the carts or the creek bank."),
        closings: ("The camera shows {D} pushing carts toward the creek, nine were found there, and after {PRIOR} {DL} knew what this costs a store.", "A dare among friends is a foolish act, not a plan to ruin carts. The State must prove {D} meant to damage them, and a joke gone wrong is not the intent the law requires."),
        timeline: [(0, "10 p.m.: {DL} reaches the bank."), (1, "The manager finds carts missing.")],
        identified: "Security Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let bowlingAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.bowlingAgain",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Bowler Back in Court After Another League Night"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace by fighting and threatening in a public bowling alley, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} shouted and threw a ball at another alley over a score.",
        state: [E(.statement, 3, "Alley Manager", "{D} shouted and threw a ball.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Heated", "{DL} says it was league banter.")],
        role: "Alley manager",
        exam: [.direct("What is your position at the alley?", "\"I'm the manager of the bowling alley, which means I run the front desk, the lanes, and the snack bar on league nights.\""), .direct("What happened on league night?", "\"{DL} got into an argument over a score with a player in the next lane, and the argument grew louder until people stopped bowling.\""), .direct("What did you hear?", "\"I heard {DL} shouting that the other player was cheating, and then I heard a threat about what would happen in the parking lot.\""), .direct("What did {DL} do with the ball?", "\"{D.He} picked up a ball and threw it down the other player's lane, sending it clattering into the pins while the player was still standing there.\""), .direct("Did anyone get hurt?", "\"Nobody was hit, but a few people near the lane jumped back, and the other player was clearly frightened.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I walked over, told {DL} to calm down, and asked {D.him} to leave, and when {D.he} didn't I called the sheriff's office.\""), .cross("The two had been playing in the same league?", "\"Yes, they were on different teams, and there has been some rivalry between those two teams all season.\""), .cross("A lot of loud talk is normal at the alley, isn't it?", "\"Some of it is, but this crossed a line when the ball was thrown and the threat was made.\""), .cross("The ball didn't hit anyone?", "\"No, it went down the lane and hit the pins, though it could have struck someone if they had been closer.\""), .cross("{DL} left when deputies arrived?", "\"{D.He} was still in the lobby, and {D.he} walked out quietly with the deputy.\""), .cross("The other player didn't want to press charges?", "\"I think {V.he} was upset, but it was my decision as the manager to call, since it disturbed the whole alley.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} disturbed the alley again.", "Banter."),
        allocution: "\"I lost my temper over a score, and I shouted things I would never say if I'd stopped to think. I rolled that ball hard when I should have walked away. Nobody was struck, but I scared people who only came out for a Friday night. I'm sorry to the manager and to everyone who had to leave the lanes.\"",
        truths: ("Two lanes cleared.", "A teammate calmed {DL}."),
        defendant: [.direct("What happened over the score?", "\"The other player recorded a frame for {V.himself} that I thought was wrong, and I said so, and we both got loud.\""), .direct("Did you threaten the other player?", "\"I said something about settling it outside. It was banter that went too far, and I didn't mean to harm anyone.\""), .direct("Why did you throw the ball?", "\"I was angry and I rolled it down the lane to make a point. I was not aiming at the other player.\""), .direct("What do you remember of the manager?", "\"The manager came over and asked me to leave. I'd already calmed down by then, and I went toward the door.\""), .direct("Did you plan to fight?", "\"No. I've never planned a fight at that alley. I'm there for the league and for the friends I've made.\""), .direct("What would you tell the manager and the players?", "\"I'm sorry I ruined the night for everyone, and I'll apologize to the other player in person if {V.he}'ll hear it.\""), .cross("You've been in court for something like this before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I told myself I'd stay calm in public. I failed to keep that promise on that night.\""), .cross("Saying you'll settle it outside sounds like a threat, doesn't it?", "\"I can see how it sounded, and I'm sorry. Where I come from it's trash talk, but others can take it differently.\""), .cross("Throwing a ball at another lane could have hurt someone, couldn't it?", "\"It could have, and I know I was lucky no one was standing in the way.\""), .cross("You were drinking that night?", "\"I had two beers, and I won't use that as an excuse, because I was in control of what I did.\""), .cross("You'll avoid league night until things settle?", "\"Yes, I'll sit out a few weeks and talk to the league about whether I should come back at all.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} got into an argument over a score with a player in the next lane, the shouting grew until people stopped bowling, and {D} threw a ball, according to the alley manager, and {DL} had faced this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say it was ordinary league banter, loud but friendly, and the ball slipped. {D} did not mean to hurt anyone."),
        closings: ("The manager watched the argument grow and the ball thrown, and after {PRIOR} {DL} knew what happens when league night turns heated.", "League banter between bowlers is not disorderly conduct, and a ball that slips from a hand is an accident. The State must prove {D} meant to disturb the alley and not merely that voices rose."),
        timeline: [(0, "The score dispute."), (0, "A deputy arrives.")],
        identified: "Alley Manager",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let tabAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.tabAgain",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Another Bar Tab Skipped"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole bar service valued at $70 belonging to {V}, a bar, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} left a different bar without paying a $70 tab.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Open Tab", "A $70 tab under {D}'s name.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Meant to Pay", "{DL} says {D.he} went to get cash.")],
        role: "Bartender",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I tend bar at a neighborhood bar, and on weeknights I'm often the only bartender working the floor.\""), .direct("What happened with {DL}'s tab?", "\"{DL} ordered drinks and food through the evening and ran up a tab of seventy dollars that was never paid.\""), .direct("How do you keep track of tabs?", "\"We open a tab in the register under the customer's name, and the card or ID is held until the tab is paid.\""), .direct("Did {DL} leave a card?", "\"No, {D.he} said {D.he} would pay in cash at the end, so we didn't hold anything for the tab.\""), .direct("When did {DL} leave?", "\"I turned to serve another customer, and when I looked back the stool was empty and the door was closing.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say about it afterward?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} left to get cash from {D.his} car and meant to come back before closing.\""), .cross("Bar tabs sometimes stay open for a long time, don't they?", "\"Sometimes, but customers normally tell us they're stepping out, and {DL} said nothing to me.\""), .cross("{DL} came in on another night?", "\"No, I haven't seen {D.him} in the bar since that night.\""), .cross("You didn't follow {DL} outside?", "\"I couldn't leave the bar unattended, so I called the owner and then the sheriff's office.\""), .cross("The tab is under {DL}'s name?", "\"Yes, the register shows the tab opened under {D.his} name with a timestamp for each round.\""), .cross("Seventy dollars isn't a large tab?", "\"No, but it's about what I'd make in tips on a good night, so it matters to me.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} skipped another tab.", "A cash run."),
        allocution: "\"I stepped out to find an ATM because I was short, and the one nearby was broken, so the bar was closed by the time I got back. I left my card behind because I meant to return. I'm sorry that it looked like I ran out on the bartender. I would have paid that tab the next day.\"",
        truths: ("The card was left behind.", "The ATM was broken."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you leave without paying?", "\"I went out to my car for cash, and I got a call from my sister and ended up driving to her place.\""), .direct("Did you intend to pay the tab?", "\"Yes, I meant to pay it. I was embarrassed that I'd left without a word, and I put off going back.\""), .direct("How did you plan to pay?", "\"I had about eighty dollars in my glove box, which I knew was enough to cover the tab and a tip.\""), .direct("Why didn't you call the bar?", "\"I didn't have the number, and I was worried I'd be told to stay away, so I let it slide.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy contacted you?", "\"I told him the truth about the cash and my sister, and I said I'd pay everything I owed.\""), .direct("What would you tell the bartender?", "\"I'm sorry for leaving you with an unpaid tab. I'll pay seventy dollars and a tip, and I'll apologize to your face.\""), .cross("You've left a bar without paying before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and that's why this looks like a habit instead of a slip. I should have paid before leaving.\""), .cross("Why not give the bartender your card first?", "\"I should have, and I'll hand my card over any time I open a tab from now on.\""), .cross("You were gone for days with no word?", "\"I was, and I regret that. I had time to come back and I put it off.\""), .cross("You have the money with you today?", "\"Yes, I brought seventy dollars and a little extra, and I'd like to pay it before I leave this courthouse.\""), .cross("You won't go back to that bar?", "\"Not until I've paid, and then I'll only go back if the owner says I'm welcome.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} ordered drinks and food all evening at a neighborhood bar and left a $70 tab unpaid, with the open tab in {D}'s name, and {DL} had been before this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say {D} went out to get cash from a machine and meant to come back and pay. {D} never planned to skip the bill."),
        closings: ("The tab is in {D}'s name and was never paid, and after {PRIOR} {DL} understood exactly what leaving a bar without settling the bill means to the person behind it.", "A cash run is not a theft, and {D} meant to return. The State must prove {D} never meant to settle the tab when {D.he} walked out of the bar."),
        timeline: [(0, "The tab opens."), (1, "The bartender checks the card.")],
        identified: "Open Tab",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let tiresAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.tiresAgain",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Seller Of 'New' Tires Back With a Different Customer"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained $380 from {V} by false pretenses, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} sold another customer used tires as new for $380.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Shop Report", "The tires were recapped.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Supplier", "{DL} says a supplier shipped used tires.")],
        role: "Tire shop owner",
        exam: [.direct("What is your business?", "\"I own a small tire shop where we sell new and used tires and mount and balance them for customers.\""), .direct("How did {DL} deal with a customer of yours?", "\"{DL} sold a set of tires to one of my customers as brand new, for three hundred eighty dollars, and they turned out to be used.\""), .direct("How did you find out?", "\"The customer brought the tires to me for an alignment, and I saw the tread wear and the date codes right away.\""), .direct("What did you see on the tires?", "\"They were recapped, with worn sidewalls, and the date code showed they were manufactured years before they were sold as new.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I wrote up a shop report with photos of the sidewalls and the date codes and gave a copy to the customer and to the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said a supplier shipped used tires by mistake and that {D.he} didn't check each one before selling them.\""), .cross("Recapped tires are legal to sell, aren't they?", "\"They are, if they're labeled as recapped, but these were sold as new and no label was on the invoice.\""), .cross("You can't say what {DL} knew?", "\"No, I can only say what the tires showed and what the invoice said. {DL}'s knowledge is something I can't see.\""), .cross("Suppliers do make mistakes?", "\"They do, and I've had shipments with the wrong tires myself, but we always check each tire before it goes on a car.\""), .cross("The tires were safe to drive on?", "\"They were legal, but they wouldn't have lasted nearly as long, so the customer overpaid.\""), .cross("You looked at the paperwork?", "\"I read the invoice, and it described the tires as new with a new-tire price, which is why we think the sale was a misrepresentation.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold used tires as new again.", "A supplier error."),
        allocution: "\"I told that customer the tires were new, and the receipt said so, and I stand by what I believed when I wrote it. I know the paperwork is gone and that makes this hard for everyone to sort out. I'm sorry that {V.he} feels cheated. I run an honest shop, and I'd make it right if I knew how.\"",
        truths: ("The receipt said new.", "No invoice exists."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did you buy those tires?", "\"I bought a pallet of tires from a wholesaler I'd used for years, and they were labeled as new when they arrived.\""), .direct("Did you inspect each tire?", "\"I looked at a few when they came in, but I didn't check every date code. I trusted the supplier's paperwork.\""), .direct("Did you know they were recapped?", "\"No, I didn't know. If I had, I would have sold them at a lower price and told the customer exactly what they were.\""), .direct("What did you do when you learned of it?", "\"I called the supplier, who admitted shipping the wrong lot, and I offered the customer a refund as soon as I knew.\""), .direct("Have you refunded the customer?", "\"I offered, but the customer wanted to go through the court first, so I haven't been able to hand over the money.\""), .direct("What would you tell the customer and the shop owner?", "\"I'm sorry for the problem. I didn't mean to sell used tires as new, and I'll refund the three hundred eighty dollars.\""), .cross("You've been accused of selling used tires as new before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I told myself I'd inspect every tire after that. I didn't do it this time, and I'm sorry.\""), .cross("A tire dealer should check date codes, shouldn't he?", "\"Yes, and I failed to do that. It's the basic thing a dealer is expected to do.\""), .cross("The supplier can confirm your story?", "\"I think so, and I'll give you the supplier's name and the invoice for that pallet if the court asks.\""), .cross("You'll refund the full amount?", "\"Yes, all three hundred eighty dollars, and I'll replace the tires at no charge if the customer wants them.\""), .cross("You'll inspect each tire in future?", "\"I will, and I'll keep a log of every date code with the customer's invoice so there's a record.\"")],
        openings: ("A customer bought a set of tires from {D} as brand new for $380, and the shop's report shows they were recapped, and {DL} had stood in this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say a supplier shipped used tires by mistake and {D} did not know. {D} sold what the supplier sent."),
        closings: ("The shop's report shows recapped tires sold as new for $380, and after {PRIOR} {DL} knew what a customer is paying for when the receipt says brand new.", "A supplier's mistake is not {D}'s fraud, and {D} sold what the supplier sent as the supplier described it. The State must prove {D} knew the tires were used when {D.he} sold them."),
        timeline: [(0, "The sale."), (0, "A shop checks.")],
        identified: "Shop Report",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let mowAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.mowAgain",
