        headlines: ["Lawn Crew Takes Prepayment Again"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained $300 from {V} by false pretenses, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} took a $300 prepayment for lawn care and never came.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Texts", "{D} promises a mow.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Weather", "{DL} says rain delayed it.")],
        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("What arrangement did you have with {DL}?", "\"I hired {DL} to mow my lawn and trim the hedges for the season, and I paid three hundred dollars up front.\""), .direct("Why did you pay in advance?", "\"{DL} said {D.he} needed the money to buy fuel and replace a mower blade, and {D.he} promised to start the next weekend.\""), .direct("What do your texts show?", "\"They show {DL} promising several times to come by on a specific day, and each time saying something else came up.\""), .direct("How long did you wait?", "\"Almost six weeks, and my grass grew so long that my neighbor complained and the town sent me a notice.\""), .direct("Did {DL} ever mow?", "\"No, {D.he} never came even once, and eventually {D.he} stopped answering my calls and texts.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say about it?", "\"{D.He} said rain kept delaying the job and that {D.he} meant to come as soon as the weather cleared.\""), .cross("It did rain some during those weeks, didn't it?", "\"Some days, yes, but there were plenty of dry days too, and {DL} didn't show up on any of them.\""), .cross("{DL} offered to refund you?", "\"{D.He} said so once in a text, but no money ever arrived.\""), .cross("Other customers have had trouble with {DL}?", "\"I heard from a neighbor that {D.he} took a deposit from another household and didn't come either.\""), .cross("You can't say why {DL} didn't come?", "\"No, I only know {D.he} didn't, and that {D.he} kept my three hundred dollars.\""), .cross("The town fined you for the grass?", "\"They sent a notice and I paid a small fine, which I put on top of what I'd paid {DL}.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took prepayments again.", "A rainy week."),
        allocution: "\"I took that money fully intending to mow, and then the rain set in and the work piled up behind. I should have called the homeowner and said so instead of letting it go quiet. That was careless of me, and I'm sorry for leaving {V.him} waiting. I will repay what was paid, every dollar, as soon as the court allows.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold the mower.", "It was dry."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the three hundred dollars?", "\"Yes, I took the money as a deposit, and I used it to cover a late truck payment that week.\""), .direct("Why didn't you mow the lawn?", "\"I got behind with other jobs, and then my mower broke, and I couldn't afford to fix it right away.\""), .direct("Did you tell the homeowner the truth?", "\"Not at first. I blamed the weather because I was embarrassed, and I'm sorry I told {V.him} something that wasn't fully true.\""), .direct("Did you plan to take the money and not work?", "\"No. I meant to do the job, and I thought I'd catch up. I can see I didn't handle it honestly.\""), .direct("Why didn't you refund the money?", "\"I didn't have it, and I was ashamed. I should have called and told {V.him} instead of avoiding {V.him}.\""), .direct("What would you tell the homeowner?", "\"I'm sorry for keeping your money and for the trouble with the town. I'll repay all three hundred dollars.\""), .cross("You've been convicted of taking prepayment before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I told the judge then I'd never take money without the work being done. I broke that promise.\""), .cross("You said it was rain when it wasn't, right?", "\"Partly. The rain was real some days, but it wasn't the reason I stayed away.\""), .cross("You spent the deposit on a truck payment?", "\"I did, and I know that's not what it was for. I should have asked first.\""), .cross("How will you pay the homeowner back?", "\"I can pay a hundred dollars now and the rest in two payments over the next month.\""), .cross("Will you stop taking deposits?", "\"Yes, I'll only take payment after the work is done, and I'll put every agreement in writing.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} took $300 up front to mow {V}'s lawn and trim the hedges for the season, promised to start the next weekend, and never came, and {DL} had already appeared here in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say rain delayed the work and {D} meant to come when the weather cleared. {D} did not mean to cheat anyone."),
        closings: ("The texts show {D} promised to mow and {V} paid three hundred dollars in advance, and with {PRIOR} behind {D.him}, {DL} knew what a prepayment is and what it obliges.", "A rainy week is not a scheme to cheat, and {D} still meant to do the work when the weather cleared. The State must prove {D} never intended to mow when {D.he} took the money."),
        timeline: [(-14, "{V} pays."), (0, "{V} calls {D}.")],
        identified: "Texts",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let formulaAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.formulaAgain",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Formula Taken From Another Pharmacy"],
        law: "larcenyMerchant",
        spec: "Took infant formula valued at $150 from {V}, a pharmacy, without paying, on {DATE}.",
