        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Need", "{DL} says {D.he} has no money.")],
        role: "Pharmacist",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role at the pharmacy?", "\"I'm the pharmacist on duty, and I'm also responsible for loss prevention in the front of the store.\""), .direct("What did you notice?", "\"I saw {DL} standing in the baby aisle for several minutes, looking around and picking up cans of infant formula.\""), .direct("What did {DL} do with the formula?", "\"{D.He} put several cans into the inside of {D.his} coat, buttoned it, and walked toward the exit.\""), .direct("How much was it worth?", "\"About one hundred fifty dollars in total, which is a lot for formula because the cans are expensive.\""), .direct("What does the aisle camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} placing each can inside the coat and glancing at the door before leaving the aisle.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say when you stopped {D.him}?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} had no money for formula and that {D.his} baby was at home waiting to be fed.\""), .cross("{DL} didn't try to run?", "\"No, {D.he} stopped as soon as I spoke and handed the cans over without any struggle.\""), .cross("There are programs that give out formula, aren't there?", "\"Yes, and I told {DL} about a few of them after the deputy arrived.\""), .cross("{DL} seemed upset?", "\"Very much so. {D.He} was close to tears and kept saying {D.he} didn't know what else to do.\""), .cross("The cans were recovered and resold?", "\"They were all returned to the shelf, since none were opened.\""), .cross("You've seen {DL} in the store before?", "\"I've seen {D.him} a few times, but I don't know if {D.he} ever bought formula here.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took formula again.", "A hungry baby."),
        allocution: "\"I have a baby at home, and I was out of formula and out of money with a payday days away. I put those cans in my coat because I was desperate, and I know that does not make it right. I'm sorry to the pharmacy. I should have gone to the shelter that offered help, and I'm asking for the chance to do better.\"",
