        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I'm a school resource officer, and I patrol the grounds and lots during school events and games.\""), .direct("What did you notice at the event?", "\"During a football game, I saw {DL}'s car parked at the edge of the lot and smelled marijuana as I walked past.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I asked {DL} to step out, and I asked for permission to look in the car, and {D.he} said yes.\""), .direct("What did you find?", "\"A marijuana cigarette in the ash tray of the center console, partly burned, along with a lighter.\""), .direct("Where was it found?", "\"In the front of the car near where {DL} had been sitting, within easy reach of the driver's seat.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said a friend left it in the car and that {D.he} hadn't looked in the ash tray in days.\""), .cross("The cigarette was in the ash tray?", "\"Yes, in plain view once the car door was open.\""), .cross("{DL} gave permission to search?", "\"Yes, {D.he} said yes when I asked, and {D.he} stood back while I looked.\""), .cross("A passenger had been in the car?", "\"{DL} said so, but I couldn't confirm who it was.\""), .cross("{DL} wasn't impaired?", "\"I saw no signs of impairment, and {D.he} was calm and polite.\""), .cross("The cigarette was tested?", "\"It was sent to the lab, and the result was positive for marijuana.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} had marijuana again.", "A friend's leftover."),
        allocution: "\"The marijuana in that car was not mine, and I told the officer so on the spot. I gave a friend a ride that night and did not look at what was left behind. I understand why it looked bad at a school event, and I'm sorry for putting the officer in that position. I'll be more careful about who rides with me.\"",
        truths: ("A second butt was in the tray.", "The friend rode."),
