        role: "Bike owner",
        exam: [.direct("What was taken from you?", "\"A mountain bicycle worth about three hundred dollars that I kept chained on my porch, which I use to ride to work.\""), .direct("When did you notice it was gone?", "\"One morning I came out to leave for work and the chain was cut and lying on the boards where the bike had been.\""), .direct("How did you find it?", "\"A friend saw it for sale at a flea market a few days later and sent me a picture of the bike and the vendor's table.\""), .direct("What does the vendor's receipt show?", "\"It shows that {DL} sold the bike to a buyer for one hundred dollars, with {D.his} name written at the bottom.\""), .direct("Did you give {DL} permission to take it?", "\"No, I know {DL} as a neighbor, but I never lent {D.him} the bike or said {D.he} could use it.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said the bike was a gift from me and that I'd told {D.him} {D.he} could keep it.\""), .cross("You and {DL} are neighbors?", "\"Yes, our houses are about a block apart, and we've said hello many times.\""), .cross("You've lent {DL} tools before?", "\"Once or twice, but never a bike and never anything {D.he} could sell.\""), .cross("The chain was cut by someone?", "\"Yes, it was cut cleanly, and I found the pieces on the porch.\""), .cross("You have a record of owning the bike?", "\"I have the receipt from the shop where I bought it and the serial number, which matches the one on the recovered bike.\""), .cross("The buyer gave the bike back?", "\"Yes, the buyer returned it once the deputy explained, and I got it back with a scratch on the frame.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold a borrowed bike again.", "A gift."),
        allocution: "\"I truly believed that bike was given to me, and I sold it at the flea market to cover rent that month. I understand now that the owner never agreed to that, and I'm sorry that I did not check. It was a kid's ride to work, and I can see what it cost. I want to pay it back.\"",
        truths: ("The frame was engraved.", "No one saw a gift."),
