        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Slow Driver", "{DL} says the car was slow.")],
        role: "Driver",
        exam: [.direct("Where were you driving?", "\"I was driving home on a two-lane highway in the evening with my two children in the back seat.\""), .direct("What did {DL} do?", "\"A pickup truck came up very close behind me and stayed there, right on my bumper, for about four miles.\""), .direct("How close was it?", "\"About a car length or less, even at fifty-five miles an hour, which meant I couldn't brake safely if I had to.\""), .direct("What does your dash camera show?", "\"It shows the truck's grille filling the rear view, then flashing its lights and moving back and forth within the lane.\""), .direct("How did you feel?", "\"I was scared for my children. I tried to speed up and then slow down, and nothing made {D.him} back off.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say afterward?", "\"{D.He} said I was driving too slowly and that {D.he} was only trying to get me to speed up.\""), .cross("You were driving below the limit?", "\"I was going about fifty, which is five under the limit, because it was getting dark.\""), .cross("There was a double yellow line?", "\"Yes, for most of those four miles, so {D.he} couldn't pass.\""), .cross("{DL} never touched your car?", "\"No, there was no contact, but it came very close at one point.\""), .cross("You pulled over eventually?", "\"I turned into a gas station, and {D.he} drove past without stopping.\""), .cross("You called the sheriff's office?", "\"I called from the gas station and gave them the plate from my camera.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove recklessly again.", "A slow driver."),
        allocution: "\"I was stuck behind a slow car and I let my frustration get the better of me. I stayed too close for far too long, and I know that could have caused a crash. I'm sorry to the driver in front of me, who was only following the limit. I've learned to give space and wait my turn.\"",
