        allocution: "\"I bought that trailer from someone I trusted, and I didn't know where it came from. I lost the bill of sale when I moved, and I understand that makes it hard for the court. I'm sorry for the owner, who lost something {V.he} needed to work. I would not knowingly take another person's equipment.\"",
