        openings: ("A stop sign and two road name signs, valued at about $250, were removed from county roads, and three signs were found in {D}'s apartment, and {DL} had been before this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say a friend gave {D} the signs as decor and {D} did not know where they came from. {D} did not take any sign."),
        closings: ("Three county signs were found in {D}'s apartment, including a stop sign, and since {PRIOR}, {DL} could not have missed what those signs are and where they belong.", "A gift from a friend is not a theft, and {D} never took any sign from any road. The State must prove {D} knew the signs were stolen when {D.he} accepted them."),
        timeline: [(0, "The signs vanish."), (2, "A tip.")],
        identified: "Signs",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"])

