        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Loan", "{DL} says {D.he} meant to repay.")],
        role: "Club president",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role in the club?", "\"I'm the president of a youth club that runs after-school activities, and members pay small dues each month.\""), .direct("Who handled the money?", "\"{DL} was elected treasurer and had sole access to the club's checking account and the debit card.\""), .direct("What did you find?", "\"When we audited the account, nine hundred dollars in dues was missing, with payments to utilities and a store that had nothing to do with the club.\""), .direct("What do the bank records show?", "\"They show withdrawals and card charges paying {DL}'s personal bills, including a phone bill and a car payment.\""), .direct("How did you confirm it was {DL}'s bills?", "\"The account numbers on the payments matched documents in {DL}'s name that the bank was able to provide.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} meant to repay it like a loan and that {D.he} hadn't intended to keep the money.\""), .cross("{DL} had permission to use the account?", "\"Only for club expenses. No one voted on any loan.\""), .cross("The money was repaid?", "\"No, not yet, though {DL} has promised to.\""), .cross("{DL} was a good treasurer before this?", "\"I thought so, and {D.he} kept clean records for most of the year.\""), .cross("The club operates on small budgets?", "\"Yes, and nine hundred dollars is a big share of our year.\""), .cross("You voted to remove {DL}?", "\"Yes, at a special meeting, and {D.he} gave up the debit card without argument.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used club money again.", "A loan."),
        allocution: "\"I spent that money on my bills when I was in a tight spot, and I meant it as a loan I'd pay back soon. I never asked the club for permission, and that was my failing. I'm sorry to the kids and the families who gave their dues. I'll repay all of it, and I'll never hold anyone's money again.\"",
