        openings: ("{D}, treasurer of another youth club with sole access to the checking account and debit card, spent $900 in club dues on personal bills, and the bank records show it, and this was not {DL}'s first time here, after {PRIOR} in {PRIORDATE}.", "The defense will say it was a loan and {D} meant to repay every dollar of it to the club. {D} never hid the spending and kept records of what {D.he} took."),
        closings: ("The bank records show club money paying {D}'s own bills, and after {PRIOR} {DL} knew exactly what a treasurer's duty is and who the dues belong to.", "A loan that {D} meant to repay is not an embezzlement, and {D} kept records of what was borrowed. The State must prove {D} meant to keep the club's money."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The dues come in."), (0, "The balance is short.")],
