        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Bought", "{DL} says {D.he} bought it.")],
        role: "Student",
        exam: [.direct("What was taken?", "\"My electric bike, worth about eight hundred dollars, which I locked outside the library while studying.\""), .direct("How was it taken?", "\"The cable lock was cut with a tool, and the bike was gone when I came out, with the pieces of the lock on the ground.\""), .direct("How did you find it?", "\"A friend of mine saw an online listing for a bike that looked exactly like mine and sent me the link.\""), .direct("What does the online listing show?", "\"A photo of my bike with the same sticker on the frame and a scratch on the fender, listed under {DL}'s account.\""), .direct("What was the price?", "\"Four hundred dollars, which is half of what the bike is worth, and the post said 'quick sale.'\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} bought the bike from someone and that {D.he} planned to sell it for a small profit.\""), .cross("The listing doesn't mention you?", "\"No, it only describes the bike and gives {DL}'s contact.\""), .cross("You sent {DL} a message?", "\"Yes, as a buyer, and {D.he} agreed to meet at a store parking lot.\""), .cross("{DL} brought the bike?", "\"Yes, with a deputy waiting nearby, and the bike was recovered.\""), .cross("Many e-bikes look the same?", "\"Some do, but my bike has a unique sticker and a scratch that match.\""), .cross("You have the serial number?", "\"Yes, from my receipt, and it matches the one on the frame.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold a stolen e-bike again.", "A purchase."),
        allocution: "\"I bought that e-bike from a seller online and I paid fair money for it. I never saw the cut cable until later, and I have no receipt because none was given. I'm sorry to the student who lost the bike, and I'd like to get it back to {V.him}. I did not steal it.\"",
