        role: "Server",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I'm a server at a restaurant, and I wait on tables and clear them during the dinner rush.\""), .direct("What happened at the table?", "\"A customer left a phone on a table by the window when they went to the restroom, and I saw it as I passed.\""), .direct("What did {DL} do?", "\"{DL}, sitting at the next table, reached over and pocketed the phone and then went back to {D.his} meal.\""), .direct("What does the restaurant camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} glancing around, sliding the phone off the table, and putting it into a jacket pocket.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I told my manager, and when the customer came back and found the phone gone, we checked the video and called the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} was going to turn the phone in at the end of the meal and hadn't taken it to keep.\""), .cross("{DL} stayed in the restaurant after?", "\"Yes, {D.he} finished {D.his} meal and paid before the deputy arrived.\""), .cross("The phone was still in the pocket?", "\"Yes, the deputy found it there, powered on.\""), .cross("{DL} didn't try to leave quickly?", "\"No, {D.he} acted calmly the entire time.\""), .cross("Customers do leave things behind?", "\"Often, and we put them in a box at the host stand.\""), .cross("{DL} didn't ask you about it?", "\"No, {D.he} never mentioned it to me or any other staff member.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a phone again.", "A turn-in."),
        allocution: "\"I picked that phone up to turn it in, and I carried it out because the battery was dead and I wasn't sure who to give it to. I should have handed it to the server on the spot. I'm sorry for the worry it caused the owner. I'd have returned it, and I'll make that happen now.\"",
